body:
@Alex2782 one approach to investigate is whether we can differentiate whether the activity is going to be recreated or not.

At the moment when the activity is recreated, the previous native instance is still around and so the crash occurs because we're attempting to initialize native objects when they already exist. 
Instead of recreating things, we should cache the existing `Godot` instance when we detect the activity will be recreated, and reuse that on restart.
